&lt;div class=&quot;c-message_actions__container c-message__actions&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Are Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer&quot; data-start=&quot;260&quot; data-end=&quot;820&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We are seeking an experienced Platform Engineer to partner directly with Lightning customers to architect, build, and deploy production AI systems. &lt;/strong&gt;Working alongside customer engineering teams, you&#39;ll solve complex technical challenges across inference infrastructure, distributed systems, APIs, and AI workflows—building reliable, observable systems that perform at scale. You&#39;ll translate customer requirements into production-ready software, turn bespoke solutions into reusable platform capabilities, and help shape the evolution of the Lightning Platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;825&quot; data-end=&quot;1210&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for a highly technical, customer-oriented platform engineer who thrives in fast-moving, ambiguous environments where success requires deep software engineering expertise, sound systems thinking, and the ability to collaborate directly with customer engineering teams to bring complex AI applications into production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This role is based in one of our hubs (New York City, San Francisco, Seattle, or London), with a minimum of 2 in-office days per week and occasional team and company offsites.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
